  "title": "Maurya Empire",
  "summary": "The Maurya Empire, founded by Chandragupta Maurya with its capital at Pataliputra (modern Patna), was the first great imperial state of South Asia. Under Ashoka it reached from the north-west frontier across much of India and he promoted Buddhism. It lasted from about 322 to 185 BCE; sources vary by a year or two.",
